&#x27;MARSHAL IS NO MORE&#x27;

&#x27;Today at six o&#x27;clock, the Shogunate&#x27;s liaison council announced the passing of His Highness Moriuji Ashikaga, Senior Third Rank, Lord General of the Six Guards.&#x27;

&#x27;When His Highness passed, why His Highness passed—on these matters no explanation whatsoever has been supplied. Only this much has been conveyed: His Highness Shirou Kuniuji, the late Lord General&#x27;s eldest grandson, is to enter the main keep of Fudaraku Castle and conduct government affairs in his place.&#x27;

&#x27;Confusion prevails in every quarter. Kyoto conspiracy, occupation-force intrigue, revenge by Okabe remnants—rumours are arriving from all directions. The continuing closure of Hachimangu since the recent sword-offering pilgrimage is also being connected to the affair, although&#x27;

&#x27;no theory possesses anything that could properly be called evidence. Speculation remains speculation.&#x27;

&#x27;However, informed sources maintain that the Lord General was in unquestionably good health. If correct, this would make illness an unlikely explanation, and some human intervention in the passing must be suspected.&#x27;

